  - /assets/js/text-rotator.js
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{# ================================================================
   HOME — Hallmark redesign pass (single-page, in-place; glass system kept).
   Pre-emit critique: P5 H4 E4 S4 R4 V4

   The old page asked "which side are you on?" three times in a row — the hero
   rotator, a dual-path benefits split, and a separate tabbed process section —
   and ran four consecutive sections with an identical head + padding block.

   Changes:
   · The dual-path split and the process tabs are now ONE stateful module: pick
     your path once and that choice drives the benefits AND the timeline. Cuts a
     whole redundant section and most of the page height.
   · Section rhythm varies: the fork is a full-width tabbed panel with no section
     head competing with it; services drop to a 2x2 card grid + one full-width
     router row (no more orphaned 5th tile); the standing policy shrinks to a
     quiet rule strip inside a single glass pane instead of a third big heading.
   · Contrast fixes: body/step/benefit copy moved off ink/55-60 (fails AA at
     these sizes per THEME.md) to ink/70; the audience line is now file-tag chips.
   · Hero stat strip gated — stats.json is placeholder. Restore when the figures
     are real and confirmed. count-up.js / logo-fallback.js dropped with it.
   · Every proof block on placeholder data stays gated (employer wall, growth
     table, traced case study, signed statements, live feed). See the TODOs.
   ================================================================ #}

